From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: tear NSS offload down after the crash-path IRQ quiesce

The NSS series inserts ath11k_nss_teardown() at the top of
ath11k_core_reconfigure_on_crash(). With this repository's 953 patch the
same function now disables the host datapath/CE interrupts on the firmware
crash path, and the donor hunk (applied with fuzz 2) lands before that, so
the offload was released while ring and CE handlers could still run -
the failure class 953 exists to prevent. Move the teardown after the quiesce.

ath11k_nss_tx_desc_mem_free() keyed its loop on tx_desc_paddr[] but only
cleared the virtual address, so a teardown after a failed re-setup (for
example an allocation failure during crash recovery) would free the pages of
the previous setup a second time. Clear the physical address and size too.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
@@ -2415,9 +2415,6 @@
 
 	mutex_lock(&ab->core_lock);
 
-	ath11k_nss_teardown(ab);
-	ab->nss.enabled = false;
-
 	ath11k_thermal_unregister(ab);
 
 	/*
@@ -2429,6 +2426,14 @@
 		ath11k_hif_ce_irq_disable(ab);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Tear the NSS offload down only once the host datapath interrupts are
+	 * quiesced (above), so no ring/CE handler can run against state the
+	 * teardown is releasing.
+	 */
+	ath11k_nss_teardown(ab);
+	ab->nss.enabled = false;
+
 	ath11k_dp_pdev_free(ab);
 	ath11k_spectral_deinit(ab);
 	ath11k_ce_cleanup_pipes(ab);
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -4183,6 +4183,8 @@
 				  ab->nss.tx_desc_vaddr[i],
 				  ab->nss.tx_desc_paddr[i]);
 		ab->nss.tx_desc_vaddr[i] = NULL;
+		ab->nss.tx_desc_paddr[i] = 0;
+		ab->nss.tx_desc_size[i] = 0;
 	}
 
 	ath11k_dbg(ab, ATH11K_DBG_NSS, "allocated tx desc mem freed\n");
